+# Experiment MOJOLEARN_CNN_FAST_FLAT_UPDATE (lane fx-rnn-cnn-fit, 2026-11-19; default OFF, A/B owed on the NVIDIA
+# L40S: owed-pre0867.json "cnn-flat-update"). Program.fit steps the optimizer once per trained parameter tensor
+# (train_program_control's update loop: one OP_OPT launch a tensor a minibatch; CNNClassifier's two blocks and head
+# are 6 tensors, 6 launches a step). Sequential's fit keeps every parameter in ONE flat buffer P with one flat
+# gradient buffer Gr, records each parameter as a leaf whose gradient lands in its slice of Gr (Tape.variable_into)
+# and updates all of them with ONE launch (autograd/model.mojo model_fit_state: `_param`, then
+# `opt_step(ex, cfg.opt, st, step, lr, P, Gr, s1, s2, s3, np_)`). Under the define a caller that asks for it
+# (`flat_update`, CNNClassifier's fit) gets that form here for the length of the fit: the trained tensors and their
+# moments are copied once into flat buffers, the replay reads the parameters from their slices and the backward
+# writes each gradient into its slice (replay_values_flat), one step_lr over the whole range a minibatch, and the
+# slices are copied back to the session's own buffers at the end. OP_OPT is elementwise with host scalars that are a
+# function of the step count alone, and every trained tensor of a fit shares that count (checked, else the
+# per-tensor loop stays), so every element sees the same operands: THE SAME BITS.
+# Kept on the per-tensor loop: conditional training (the trained set changes per minibatch), a stopping criterion
+# (its shadows name the session's buffers), `grads_out`, and a clipping optimizer (the clip norm is per tensor).
+# General, not a shape: any program whose caller passes `flat_update`. Launches a step for CNNClassifier's board
+# net: 6 -> 1 optimizer launches; a deeper net saves two per layer.
+comptime PROGRAM_FLAT_UPDATE = is_defined["MOJOLEARN_CNN_FAST_FLAT_UPDATE"]()
+
